<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr PPI 10.5 pct in 1996 vs 18.9 in 1995.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr PPI 10.5 pct in 1996 vs 18.9 in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish producer prices rose 0.5 percent in December against a 0.7 percent rise in November, taking year-on-year producer price inflation in 1996 up to 10.5 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>It said PPI rose 12.1 percent in the January-December period, compared with a 25.4 percent rise in the corresponding period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH PRODUCER INFLATION	  DECEMBER  NOVEMBER   DEC 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)		0.5	 0.7	 0.6</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		     10.5	10.1	18.9</p>
<p>  manufacturing m/m change	     0.5	 0.7	 0.6</p>
<p>  manufacturing yr/yr change	   9.9	10.4	19.1</p>
<p>  mining m/m change			1.1	 1.1	 0.4</p>
<p>  mining yr/yr change		   10.6	 7.8	22.9</p>
<p>  utilities m/m change		   0.1	 0.2	 0.4</p>
<p>  utilities yr/yr change		11.9	12.0	17.5</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
